      "id": 4,
      "claim": "Higher out‑of‑pocket costs are a major determinant of whether patients accept recommended diagnostic imaging.",
      "evidence": "Health‑services research (e.g., studies of the National Hospital Ambulatory Medical Care Survey) consistently finds lower rates of CT utilization among uninsured patients compared with insured patients, even after controlling for clinical need.",
